{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104900","id":2432956601,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6RA_i5","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104900","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104900.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104900.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104900","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104900/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104900/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104900/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/72d89e41b915b995ed31e146a928adf25abc7344","number":104900,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Add functions to apply forces given a global position instead of an origin offset","user":{"login":"GustJc","id":3084189,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwODQxODk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3084189?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc","html_url":"https://github.com/GustJc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"# What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Closes https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/12115\r\n\r\nAdds physics methods for `apply_force_at_position(force, world_pos)` and `apply_impulse_at_position(force, world_pos)`.\r\n\r\nWhich uses a **global coordinate position** to say where the force is applied.\r\nThey represent a more common use-case where you want to apply a force to a global position.\r\n\r\nFor example, you can apply the force at a given node's position that is attached to the player's body without having to use subtract the rigidbodies global_position.\r\nSo _apply_force(force, (global_point - global_position) )_ == _apply_force_at_position(force, global_point)_\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3e2d2628-c6a8-4ac6-a94f-71996c0b7dfe\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2d0e2358-0023-4c79-b72b-fee2048c6d04\r\n\r\n\r\n# Additional information\r\n\r\nThe **reason they are being added** is to not change/break the behavior of the already in use `apply_force` and `apply_impulse` which can take an optional global offset value for the position.\r\nSo this PR **will not break compatibility.**\r\n\r\nUsing them, it is now possible to apply forces at child objects position's without any hassle\r\n```gdscript\r\napply_force_at_position(-%ForceLeft.global_basis.y * FORCE, %ForceLeft.global_position)\r\n```\r\nPreviously, to get the same behavior you'd need to use\r\n```gdscript\r\nvar body_offset := %ForceLeft.global_position - global_position\r\napply_force(-%ForceLeft.global_basis.y * FORCE, body_offset)\r\n```\r\nWhich is **more confusing** and can lead to a lot of errors if you don't understand what a global offset means.\r\n\r\n_(My first time using godot, years ago, I read it wrong and thought it was a local offset in the same sense as a local position, so the offset would be relative to the body's rotation. Made to lose two days thinking my math was wrong and redoing stuff)_\r\n\r\n---\r\nI've made a test MRP you can play around to check if everything is working as it should. \r\nFrom my simple tests, it seems to be okay.\r\n[PR_MRP_physics_apply_at_position.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19560234/PR_MRP_physics_apply_at_position.zip)\r\n\r\nApplying forces at the red cubes when pressing left/right and space \r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3477e1ab-c4dd-4bf1-9d5c-0951c4bbf45b\r\n\r\n---\r\nFor reference, only Godot seems to use this global offset approach. \r\nWith all other engines I've researched using global coordinates instead. \r\nThis also include Jolt's own internals with AddForce(force, global_coordinate)\r\n\r\nEdit: Force pushed changes, Jolt parameters now casts to JPH::RVec3 to not break tests.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":370471880,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzNzA0NzE4ODA=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:physics","name":"topic:physics","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708289,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:3d","name":"topic:3d","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16/labels","number":16,"state":"open","title":"4.x","description":"Issues and pull requests slated for an undetermined Godot 4 release.","creator":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","ht